 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Airbus (Paris: AIR) agreed to sell its U.S. space business to Cerberus Capital Management . 

 Why it's the BFD: Airbus caught some congressional heat for allegedly providing satellite imagery of U.S. military assets to China, just ahead of the Iran war.

 Now the business not only moves into U.S. hands, but the firm was founded and previously led by Steve Feinberg — who currently serves as the Pentagon's No. 2 official behind Pete Hegseth. Zoom in: The business manufactures satellites near Florida's Kennedy Space Center for both national security and commercial customers.

 Expect the deal to close by year-end. The bottom line: "Airbus is in the process of merging its satellite operations business with Leonardo and Thales to create a European joint venture that would compete with Elon Musk's SpaceX." — Leen Al-Rashdan, Bloomberg 

 
 
